results.description:
🛰️ Scarborough Shoal, 27 Oct: The Philippine Coast Guard and Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources (MV Mamalakaya and BRP Malapascua) supplied fuel to about 40 to 50 Filipino fishing boats today. 

Their aircraft spotted vessels from the Chinese Coast Guard and the People’s Liberation Army Navy nearby, along with a Chinese research ship lurking around. But there was no fuss—everything went smoothly, and the mission was wrapped up without any issues. This spot has been effectively controlled by China since 2012, and the 2016 ruling that favored fishing access? Well, Beijing’s not on board with that. Here's a real photo from the PCG.  
@PhilCoastGuard @PhilippineNavy @USPacificFleet #WestPhilippineSea #Scarborough #OSINT

